+### Request-only memory context (review candidate)
+
+This local candidate adds `{ requiresMemoryAudience: true }` to
+`before_prompt_build` for plugins with explicitly applied
+`hooks.allowConversationAccess: true`. The host resolves the admitted session
+through the existing memory-audience owner, including non-owner conversation
+partitions. A legacy provider remains legacy; tools and sibling hooks gain no
+additional scope.
+
+Embedded prompt events use the admitted transcript recorder for
+`currentUserMessage` and its stable `currentUserMessageId`. Missing admission
+provides no identity. Prompt text, model output, transport correlation, and run IDs
+never substitute for the source.
+
+A plugin may return `ephemeralContext`, a read-only asynchronous reader receiving
+fresh `hookInvocation.assertActive()` custody for each foreground provider round.
+After a fresh exact-key plugin-state read, return `{ text, assertCurrent }` with
+live tenant, consent, audience, and plugin-instance checks. The host also retains
+source and publication checks until stream terminal. Temporary text is absent
+from transcript, `modelPromptProjection`, trajectory, compaction, and queued
+injections.
+
+Only a final-dispatch V1 contract obtained from the actual selected host factory
+permits reading and injecting context. The candidate certifies the OpenAI
+Responses, OpenAI Completions, Azure Responses, and Anthropic Messages factories.
+Unknown/custom and Google-owned provider streams have no certificate. Native
+Codex session streams retain their original route and currently receive no
+request-only memory. Their endpoint and headers are not interchangeable with the
+generic Responses factory. Already-sent fallback and client-compaction
+continuations also currently omit the original source-user fields and receive no
+memory.
+
+For certified requests, the existing guarded model HTTP owner checks current
+memory authority after asynchronous preparation and immediately before raw fetch.
+Only that owner signs the model-effect receipt; auxiliary authentication traffic
+does not. Ordinary fallback is allowed once after a specific memory refusal only
+when no model effect was initiated and no content was published. A sent or
+uncertain request is not replayed on that basis. Private scopes use the existing
+managed HTTP route rather than an unproven WebSocket send path.
+
+Ordinary fact deletion applies to subsequent turns. An already-started reply may
+use a previously read snapshot; already-sent model input is not rolled back. New
+turns after successful deletion must not recover the fact from old projections,
+queued sources, or provider continuation caches. This does not relax authorization
+revocation, tenant isolation, or any existing host assertion. Existing stricter
+publication checks remain.
+
+Readers share a 4,096 UTF-8 byte request cap, including separators and capped by
+the context-token budget. Plugins should apply a smaller relevant-fact budget.
+Errors, timeout, missing tracked reads, retirement, or exceeded budgets omit memory
+and preserve ordinary chat where its source remains authorized. The read
+capability authorizes no tools or other side effects.
+
+This is not a released capability. Source tests do not replace a rebuild and
+Gateway composition check of the final runtime. Host/SDK/security-owner review and
+an accepted compatibility version are required before distribution; the unchanged
+`2026.10.7` version alone cannot distinguish this candidate from the original host.
+
